\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The ladder on the multidimensional knapsack (MOMKP), one of the four structures of Table~\ref {tab:structures}. As on the visa problem, all three random-key methods (NSGA-II, the MOHHO swarm, and random restart) sit below the three permutation-native methods---a clean two-tier split. The split reverses only on the \emph  {sequencing} landscapes (TSP, flow-shop), where the real-coded methods become competitive (Table~\ref {tab:structures}).}}{20}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ladder2}{{9}{20}{The ladder on the multidimensional knapsack (MOMKP), one of the four structures of Table~\ref {tab:structures}. As on the visa problem, all three random-key methods (NSGA-II, the MOHHO swarm, and random restart) sit below the three permutation-native methods---a clean two-tier split. The split reverses only on the \emph {sequencing} landscapes (TSP, flow-shop), where the real-coded methods become competitive (Table~\ref {tab:structures})}{figure.9}{}}
